@urn-forge:strict
@urn:corpus:inventory:reservation:operation:reserve_stock
Feature: Reserve stock for an order

  Scenario: A reservation holds every line in full and answers RESERVED with a reservation id
    When I run the operation with:
      | idempotency_key | order_id | lines                                                                                                          |
      | res-0001        | ORD-1    | [{ sku: WIDGET-1, location: AMS-B-0142, quantity: 3 }, { sku: GADGET-2, location: ROT-A-0001, quantity: 100 }] |
    Then the output is:
      | result   | reservation_id                       | order_id | state  | lines                                                                                                          | expires_at               |
      | RESERVED | c0ffee00-1234-4abc-8def-0123456789ab | ORD-1    | ACTIVE | [{ sku: WIDGET-1, location: AMS-B-0142, quantity: 3 }, { sku: GADGET-2, location: ROT-A-0001, quantity: 100 }] | 2026-11-22T10:30:00.000Z |
    And the operation emits "urn:corpus:inventory:reservation:event:stock_reserved":
      | event_id                             | sequence | reservation_id                       | quantity_changed | level                                                                                | occurred_at              |
      | 7d3f1c2a-5b4e-4a6d-9c8b-1e2f3a4b5c6d | 1        | c0ffee00-1234-4abc-8def-0123456789ab | 3                | { sku: WIDGET-1, location: AMS-B-0142, on_hand: 500, reserved: 103, available: 397 } | 2026-11-22T10:00:00.000Z |

  Scenario Outline: A time-to-live from 1 minute to 7 days sets when the reservation expires
    When I run the operation with:
      | idempotency_key | order_id | lines                                                  | ttl_minutes   |
      | res-0002        | ORD-2    | [{ sku: WIDGET-1, location: AMS-B-0142, quantity: 1 }] | <ttl_minutes> |
    Then the output is:
      | state  | expires_at   |
      | ACTIVE | <expires_at> |

    Examples:
      | ttl_minutes | expires_at               |
      | 1           | 2026-11-22T10:01:00.000Z |
      | 10080       | 2026-11-29T10:00:00.000Z |

  Scenario Outline: A time-to-live under 1 minute or over 7 days is rejected
    When I run the operation with:
      | idempotency_key | order_id | lines                                                  | ttl_minutes   |
      | res-0002        | ORD-2    | [{ sku: WIDGET-1, location: AMS-B-0142, quantity: 1 }] | <ttl_minutes> |
    Then the input is rejected on "ttl_minutes"

    Examples:
      | ttl_minutes |
      | 0           |
      | 10081       |

  Scenario: A reservation that takes the last available unit makes the stock depleted
    When I run the operation with:
      | idempotency_key | order_id | lines                                                    |
      | res-0003        | ORD-3    | [{ sku: WIDGET-1, location: AMS-B-0142, quantity: 400 }] |
    Then the operation emits "urn:corpus:inventory:reservation:event:stock_reserved":
      | quantity_changed | level                                                                              |
      | 400              | { sku: WIDGET-1, location: AMS-B-0142, on_hand: 500, reserved: 500, available: 0 } |
    And the operation emits "urn:corpus:inventory:stock:event:stock_depleted":
      | event_id                             | sequence | sku      | location   | occurred_at              |
      | 7d3f1c2a-5b4e-4a6d-9c8b-1e2f3a4b5c6d | 1        | WIDGET-1 | AMS-B-0142 | 2026-11-22T10:00:00.000Z |

